'''Hanzo the Betrothed''' is an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] that can be obtained from the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[June Bride (Gacha Event)|June Bride]] gacha event. He is an anti-[[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]]/[[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] variant of [[Hattori Hanzo (Uber Rare Cat)|Hattori Hanzo]] and was added in [[Version 15.4 Update|Version 15.4]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 862
|rarity = UR
|name1 = Hanzo the Betrothed
|name2 = Hanzo the Groom
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Hanzo the Groom''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Just like his [[Hattori Hanzo (Uber Rare Cat)|original counterpart]], Hanzo the Groom is fantastic role compression that eviscerates targets while cutting them a one-way pass to stunlock hell. His [[Slow]] has a 74% uptime assuming all [[Fruit Treasures]], which is very good for what is otherwise a decent backline nuker in his own right. His matchups against targets are equally favorable, outranging every common Zombie save for [[Zamelle]], usually staggering them before having his Slow run out only for them to sprint into his attack again. Red isn't the best target for Hanzo, since most enemies there don't necessitate a nuker of any kind, and/or already outrange him. He's good for [[Bore]], as well as [[Two Can]] and [[Berserkory]] if you have a good Wave Shield, but that's as far as it goes.

Hanzo the Groom has above-average survivability, leveraging his offense as his primary defense to annihilate most enemies as they approach. He is still prone to Zombies burrowing into him, however, but they're likely to get sniped by his attack as they're unburrowing. His main problem in this department is enemy pierce, since he has barely any immunities, which can make him quite the sandbag in a lot of situations. Even with this, Hanzo the Groom is a great unit whose strengths outweigh his weaknesses.

{{Job|Classification = Nuker & Crowd-Controller}}

